S('app','Identity','Register an Application','Create an app object so an app can sign in users or call APIs.',2,4,'Microsoft Entra ID>Manage>App registrations>New registration','Enter <b>Name</b>.|Choose <b>Supported account types</b>.|Add a <b>Redirect URI</b> if it is a web or SPA app.|Select <b>Register</b>; note Application (client) ID and Directory (tenant) ID.|Open <b>Certificates &amp; secrets</b> and add a certificate or client secret.|Open <b>API permissions</b> → <b>Add a permission</b>; grant admin consent if required.','Overview shows IDs; sign-in test returns a token.','App registrations → Delete (restorable for 30 days).','AADSTS50011 => redirect URI mismatch.|Secret expired => create a new one and rotate.','entra/identity-platform/quickstart-register-app',[('CLI','az ad app create --display-name app-demo','Creates the registration. Needs Application Developer.')],'Prefer certificates or managed identity over secrets.|Request least-privilege permissions.','Track secret expiry; set owners.'),
S('ent','Identity','Add an Enterprise Application','Configure sign-in, assignment and SSO for an app in your tenant.',2,4,'Microsoft Entra ID>Manage>Enterprise applications>New application','Select a gallery app or <b>Create your own application</b>.|Open <b>Users and groups</b> → <b>Add user/group</b> and assign access.|Open <b>Single sign-on</b> and choose the method (SAML or OIDC).|On <b>Properties</b>, set <b>Assignment required</b> to Yes.','Test sign-in as an assigned user.','Properties → Delete.','User sees AADSTS50105 => user not assigned.|SAML error => check Entity ID and reply URL.','entra/identity/enterprise-apps/add-application-portal','','Use Conditional Access on the app.','Review consent grants regularly.'),
S('sp','Identity','Create a Service Principal for Automation','Give CI/CD or scripts an identity with scoped Azure access.',3,4,'Microsoft Entra ID>App registrations>New registration','Register an app (see Register an Application).|Add a certificate or secret under <b>Certificates &amp; secrets</b>.|On the target scope open <b>Access control (IAM)</b> → <b>Add role assignment</b> and select the app.','Sign in with the identity and run a read command.','Remove role assignment; delete the registration.','Login fails => check tenant ID, secret expiry.|Forbidden => role not assigned at the scope.','entra/identity-platform/howto-create-service-principal-portal',[('CLI','az ad sp create-for-rbac --name sp-ci --role Contributor --scopes /subscriptions/<sub-id>/resourceGroups/rg-app-dev-001','Creates app, service principal and role assignment; prints a secret once. Store it in Key Vault.')],'Prefer workload identity federation or managed identity.|Scope narrowly.','Rotate credentials; avoid Owner.'),
S('ca','Identity','Create a Conditional Access Policy (Require MFA)','Require MFA based on user, app and conditions.',3,4,'Microsoft Entra ID>Protection>Conditional Access>Policies>New policy','Enter a <b>Name</b>.|<b>Users</b>: include a pilot group; exclude emergency access accounts.|<b>Target resources</b>: choose apps (e.g. Azure management).|<b>Grant</b>: Require multifactor authentication.|Set <b>Enable policy</b> to Report-only, then <b>Create</b>.|Review sign-in logs, then switch to On.','Sign-in logs → Conditional Access tab shows policy result.','Disable or delete the policy.','Locked out => use the excluded break-glass account.|Policy not applied => check assignments and report-only state.','entra/identity/conditional-access/howto-conditional-access-policy-all-users-mfa','','Always exclude two break-glass accounts.','Needs Entra ID P1; pilot first.'),
