S('pim','Identity','Assign an Eligible Role with PIM','Give just-in-time privileged access that users activate when needed.',3,4,'Privileged Identity Management>Azure resources>Select the scope>Assignments>Add assignments','Select the <b>Role</b> and <b>Members</b>.|Set <b>Assignment type</b> to Eligible and the duration.|Select <b>Assign</b>.|User opens <b>PIM</b> → <b>My roles</b> → <b>Activate</b>, gives a reason, and activates.','Eligible tab lists the assignment; Activity shows activation.','Assignments → select → Remove.','No Activate option => assignment is not eligible or not yet started.|PIM missing => needs Entra ID P2 or Governance license.','entra/id-governance/privileged-identity-management/pim-resource-roles-assign-roles','','Require MFA and justification on activation.','Use access reviews; cap activation duration.'),
S('rt','Networking','Create a Route Table (UDR)','Override default routing, e.g. send traffic through a firewall.',2,5,'Route tables>Create','<b>Basics</b>: subscription, group, region, name.|Open <b>Settings</b> → <b>Routes</b> → <b>Add</b>: prefix, next hop type (Virtual appliance), next hop IP.|Open <b>Settings</b> → <b>Subnets</b> → <b>Associate</b> and choose the subnet.','Subnet → Effective routes shows the custom route.','Disassociate from subnets, then delete.','Traffic dropped => the appliance must allow IP forwarding.|Asymmetric routing => add return route.','virtual-network/manage-route-table',[('CLI','az network route-table route create -g rg-app-dev-001 --route-table-name rt-app -n to-fw --address-prefix 0.0.0.0/0 --next-hop-type VirtualAppliance --next-hop-ip-address 10.0.0.4','Sends all traffic to the appliance. Needs Network Contributor.')]),
S('nic','Networking','Create a Network Interface (NIC)','Create a NIC to attach to a VM.',1,5,'Network interfaces>Create','Enter name, region, <b>Virtual network</b> and <b>Subnet</b>.|Choose private IP assignment (Dynamic or Static).|Optionally attach an NSG.|Select <b>Review + create</b>.|To attach, deallocate the VM → <b>Networking</b> → <b>Attach network interface</b>.','NIC shows a private IP and attached VM.','Detach from the VM, then delete.','Attach unavailable => VM must be stopped (deallocated) and in the same region/VNet.','virtual-network/virtual-network-network-interface',[('CLI','az network nic create -g rg-app-dev-001 -n nic-app --vnet-name vnet-app-dev --subnet snet-app','Creates the NIC. Needs Network Contributor.')]),
S('pdns','Networking','Create a Private DNS Zone and Link a VNet','Resolve private names inside a VNet.',2,5,'Private DNS zones>Create','Enter the zone name (e.g. corp.local or privatelink.blob.core.windows.net).|Open <b>Settings</b> → <b>Virtual network links</b> → <b>Add</b>; pick the VNet; enable auto registration only for VM records.|Add <b>Record sets</b> if needed.','VM in the linked VNet resolves the name (nslookup).','Delete links, then the zone.','Name not resolving => zone not linked to that VNet.|Custom DNS server => forward to 168.63.129.16.','dns/private-dns-getstarted-portal',[('CLI','az network private-dns zone create -g rg-app-dev-001 -n corp.local','Creates the zone.'),('CLI','az network private-dns link vnet create -g rg-app-dev-001 -z corp.local -n link-app -v vnet-app-dev -e false','Links the VNet without auto registration.')]),
